From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] of: put back the root model and compatible a stock ABL replaced

The Retroid Pocket Duo boots through its stock Qualcomm ABL. That ABL always
applies the device's own dtbo (and the hypervisor's overlays) onto the DTB it
is given; our DTB carries an empty /abl-dtbo-sink node and a /__symbols__ node
that points every stock label at it, so every fragment is skipped and the
overlay succeeds. The overlay still merges its root properties, though: model
becomes "Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. Kera MTP + WCN7750 + UFS2" and compatible
"qcom,kera-mtp", ... Drivers that match the machine compatible then fail; the
display does not probe ("Couldn't find UBWC config data for this platform!"),
and userspace no longer sees "retroidpocket,rpduo".

The DTB keeps the real values in /abl-dtbo-sink (pbos,model and
pbos,compatible). Copy them back to the root right after unflattening, before
anything matches on them. DTBs without that node are not touched.

---
diff --git a/drivers/of/fdt.c b/drivers/of/fdt.c
--- a/drivers/of/fdt.c
+++ b/drivers/of/fdt.c
@@ -1269,6 +1269,40 @@
 		memcpy(dt, fdt, size);
 
 	return dt;
+}
+
+/*
+ * A stock Qualcomm ABL overlays its own dtbo onto our DTB and replaces the root
+ * model and compatible on the way. /abl-dtbo-sink holds the real ones. Runs
+ * before of_core_init(), so the node kobjects are not set up yet: walk the
+ * children directly instead of using the refcounting helpers.
+ */
+static void __init of_restore_abl_root_identity(void)
+{
+	static const char * const props[][2] = {
+		{ "pbos,compatible", "compatible" },
+		{ "pbos,model", "model" },
+	};
+	struct device_node *np;
+	int i;
+
+	if (!of_root)
+		return;
+	for (np = of_root->child; np; np = np->sibling)
+		if (of_node_name_eq(np, "abl-dtbo-sink"))
+			break;
+	if (!np)
+		return;
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(props); i++) {
+		struct property *src = of_find_property(np, props[i][0], NULL);
+		struct property *dst = of_find_property(of_root, props[i][1], NULL);
+
+		if (!src || !dst)
+			continue;
+		dst->value = src->value;
+		dst->length = src->length;
+	}
+	pr_info("OF: root model and compatible restored from /abl-dtbo-sink\n");
 }
 
 /**
@@ -1302,6 +1336,8 @@
 	__unflatten_device_tree(fdt, NULL, &of_root,
 				early_init_dt_alloc_memory_arch, false);
 
+	of_restore_abl_root_identity();
+
 	/* Get pointer to "/chosen" and "/aliases" nodes for use everywhere */
 	of_alias_scan(early_init_dt_alloc_memory_arch);
 
